        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A. It is the responsibility of the Board to provide safe and sanitary working conditions, including equipment, in all present and future installations, and to develop a safe working force. The MCCSSE will cooperate with and assist the administration to live up to its responsibility. The parties recognize that each unit member has a responsibility to give effect to the safety program by following the safety procedures and working to see that all safety regulations are properly implemented.",
